* **Q2(e) Complete input-space partition for the two edited case bodies (`R7` / `R7b`)** �?" **(`READ`: [cpu_ppc_instr.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4307-L4381), [ppc_dsform_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/ppc_dsform_probe.py#L46-L68), [ppc_dsform_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/ppc_dsform_probe.py#L296-L526))**
  * Partitioning the inputs seen by `case PPC_HI6_LD:` (opcode 58) and `case PPC_HI6_STD:` (opcode 62) along `opcode (58, 62) x XO (0, 1, 2, 3) x DS (<0, =0, >0) x RA (=0, !=0, RA=RT, RA=RS) x lwa word bit 31 (1, 0) x CPU width (64-bit, 32-bit)`:
    1. **Observed in the 39 rows (on 64-bit `-E bareppc -M 64`)**:
       * `ld` (`58 / XO 0`): `(DS > 0, RA != 0)` (`ld value`, `+8`), `(DS = 0, RA != 0)` (`ld ds0 value`, `+0`), `(DS > 0, RA = 0)` (`ld ra0 value`, `+0x1100`).
       * `ldu` (`58 / XO 1`): `(DS > 0, RA != 0, RA != RT)` (`ldu value`, `ldu ra`, `+16`), `(DS = 0, RA != 0, RA != RT)` (`ldu ds0 val`, `ldu ds0 ra`, `+0`), `(DS < 0, RA != 0, RA != RT)` (`ldu neg val`, `ldu neg ra`, `-16`), `(DS > 0, RA = 0)` (`ldu ra0 stop`, `+8`).
       * `lwa` (`58 / XO 2`, all with loaded 32-bit word bit 31 = `1`): `(DS > 0, RA != 0)` (`lwa pos value`, `+24`), `(DS = 0, RA != 0)` (`lwa ds0 value`, `+0`), `(DS < 0, RA != 0)` (`lwa neg value`, `-8`), `(DS > 0, RA = 0)` (`lwa ra0 value`, `+0x10f0`).
       * `opcode 58 / XO 3` (reserved): `(DS > 0, RA != 0)` (`xo58_3 stop`, `DS = +8, RA = r14`).
       * `std` (`62 / XO 0`): `(DS > 0, RA != 0)` (`std value`, `std low4`, `+8`), `(DS = 0, RA != 0)` (`std ds0 val`, `+0`), `(DS > 0, RA = 0)` (`std ra0 val`, `+0x7100`).
       * `stdu` (`62 / XO 1`): `(DS > 0, RA != 0, RA != RS)` (`stdu value`, `stdu ra`, `stdu window`, `+16`), `(DS = 0, RA != 0, RA != RS)` (`stdu ds0 val`, `stdu ds0 ra`, `stdu ds0 win`, `+0`), `(DS < 0, RA != 0, RA != RS)` (`stdu neg val`, `stdu neg ra`, `-16`), `(DS > 0, RA = 0)` (`stdu ra0 stop`, `+8`), `(DS > 0, RA = RS != 0)` (`stdu rars val`, `stdu rars ra`, `+8` with `RS = RA = r15`).
       * `opcode 62 / XO 2` (reserved): `(DS > 0, RA != 0)` (`xo62_2 stop`, `DS = +8, RA = r14`).
       * `opcode 62 / XO 3` (reserved): `(DS > 0, RA != 0)` (`xo62_3 stop`, `DS = +8, RA = r14`).
    2. **Unobserved in the 39 rows, and how each is accounted for**:
       * **`DS < 0` on `ld` (`58/0`) and `std` (`62/0`), and `DS <= 0` / `RA = 0` on reserved `58/3`, `62/2`, `62/3`**: `DS` is a `14`-bit signed displacement (`16384` values, `SAMPLED` under `R7b`). Neither `ld`/`std` nor the `default: goto bad;` branches test the sign of `imm` (`imm == 0` at [cpu_ppc_instr.c:4357](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_ppc_instr.c#L4357) only tests `== 0` vs. `!= 0`, and `default: goto bad;` exits before `:4357`), while signed negative `(int16_t)(iword & ~3)` is already directly exercised by `ldu neg val`/`ra` (`58/1`), `lwa neg value` (`58/2`), and `stdu neg val`/`ra` (`62/1`).
